hrough licensed retail liquor outlets (Annual Report 2020/21, p.2, p.4). It earns money through beer volume x price, plus royalty income from licensing its brands to Group affiliates (Annual Report 2024/25, Statement of Profit or Loss notes). Ceylon Beverage Holdings PLC is its immediate parent, with Carson Cumberbatch PLC as ultimate parent (Annual Report 2020/21, p.50). Group revenue grew from LKR 47.8Bn (FY2020) to LKR 123.4Bn (FY2025), roughly 2.6x over five years -- driven mostly by price increases passing through excise duty hikes and post-2022 currency devaluation, not volume growth (Chairman's Message, FY2021 and FY2023 Annual Reports). The single biggest swing factor on reported profit is excise/tax policy: alcohol is taxed at 40-45% versus the 30% standard corporate rate, and government tax changes move profit directly (Annual Report 2022/23, Chairman's Message).", "gaps_note": "No gaps for FY2020-FY2025 and the latest interim; all figures traced to audited Statement of Profit or Loss tables or the report's own Financial Highlights/Review pages.", "income_statement_analysis": null, "balance_sheet_analysis": null, "cash_flow_analysis": null, "equity_statement_analysis": null, "other_statements_analysis": null, "earnings_comparison": [{"period": "FY2024 (year ended 31 March 2024)", "period_end_date": "2024-03-31", "basis": "GROUP", "revenue": 109755568.0, "operating_income": 15367756.0, "pbt": 14001948.0, "pat": 8403478.0, "eps": 105.04, "currency": "LKR", "source_doc_id": "manual_20e4d7b42c753e77", "source_page": 115}, {"period": "FY2025 (year ended 31 March 2025)", "period_end_date": "2025-03-31", "basis": "GROUP", "revenue": 123431021.0, "operating_income": 16185876.0, "pbt": 15742867.0, "pat": 9508454.0, "eps": 118.86, "currency": "LKR", "source_doc_id": "manual_20e4d7b42c753e77", "source_page": 115}]}, "financials_interim": [{"id": 3, "symbol": "LION", "company_name": "Lion Brewery (Ceylon) PLC", "period_type": "INTERIM", "period_label": "Q2 FY2025/26 (