osed for this period", "net_debt_to_ebitda: one or more required inputs not disclosed for this period", "interest_coverage: one or more required inputs not disclosed for this period", "asset_turnover: one or more required inputs not disclosed for this period", "receivables_turnover: one or more required inputs not disclosed for this period", "working_capital: one or more required inputs not disclosed for this period", "free_cash_flow: one or more required inputs not disclosed for this period"]}, "revenue_growth_yoy": 0.12459917295494294, "pat_growth_yoy": 0.1314903186513965, "thesis": {"recommendation": "ACCUMULATE", "composite_score": 68.6, "thesis_text": "Lion Brewery is Sri Lanka's leading beer brewer, distributing through licensed retail liquor outlets domestically and exporting to roughly 26 countries. FY2025 Group revenue grew 12.5% and PAT 13.1%, a steadier and more proportionate growth pattern than its holding company BREW shows at the consolidated level, alongside a similar deleveraging trend (finance costs down 42.5% YoY, interest coverage roughly doubled). At 14.5x P/E and 4.01x P/B, it trades at a modest premium to BREW, consistent with being the direct operating entity rather than a holding shell. The core risk is regulatory: Sri Lankan alcohol excise policy is a recurring government revenue lever this project has no way to monitor in advance (Annual Report FY2025, p.113-115)."}}}